* Went down to the castle, used the blindfold to see if any grey
dragons were in residence (they weren't).  So I cashed my lamp
in for some blessed GDSM.
* Did the quest.  Found another magic lamp and a magic marker.
* Chucked The Tsurugi of Muramasa into a stash box and never looked at
it again.
* Masterminded the drawbridge, then played squish for a while.
* Got the WoW. Wished for 2 blessed scrolls of charging, a magic marker
and 2 blessed scrolls of enchant armour (I hadn't seen any at all).
When I got the wand I was tempted to try and convert myself to chaotic,
so I could wish for the Longbow of Diana and be an evil poison arrow
using samurai, but decided that I could just collect a bunch of arrows,
enchant them up and poison them, then ignore the dishonour message.
* I ended up with about 100 elven arrows and twice that many normal
arrows.  Since I had an abundance of marker charges I enchanted
both lots up to +7.
* Fought liches for a while, until one summoner a mindflayer that
sucked
my brain.  For retribution I wiped out both L and h.
